Batch 1 handed off at 20:23. Now start batch 2 (T16) while review runs — it's ready (independent of batch 1, same base commit).

T16 plan:
1. `src/server.py`: Accept negotiation helper + static file routes (app.css, app.js).
2. `src/ui.py`: layout renderer (Pebble brand, nav, esc helper, wants_html).
3. `src/static/app.css`: token-based design system.
4. `src/static/app.js`: shared logic module (parser, formatter, refresh guard, key derivation + sha256 fallback).
5. Tests: test_t16_negotiation.py (Accept negotiation via stub route + static routes), app.js logic tests via node, layout/CSS token smoke test.

Where should wants_html live? ui.py makes sense (UI concern). Server routes for static files: public GET routes.

Design decisions for app.js module shape:

```js
(function (root, factory) {
  if (typeof module === "object" && module.exports) {
    module.exports = factory();
  } else {
    root.Pebble = factory();
  }
})(typeof globalThis === "object" ? globalThis : this, function () {
  "use strict";

  // decimal parser: "15.00" minor 2 -> 1500
  function parseDecimalAmount(raw, minorUnits) { ... }

  function formatAmount(minor, minorUnits, currency) { ... }

  function createRefreshGuard() { let issued = 0, applied = 0; return { issue, arrive }; }

  function sha256Hex(text) -> Promise<string>  // subtle if available, else fallback

