parseDecimalAmount details:
```js
function parseDecimalAmount(raw, minorUnits) {
  if (typeof raw !== "string") return { ok: false, error: "Enter an amount" };
  var text = raw.trim();
  if (!/^\d+(\.\d+)?$/.test(text)) return { ok: false, error: "Enter a valid amount, e.g. 15.00" };
  var parts = text.split(".");
  var decimals = parts[1] ? parts[1].length : 0;
  if (decimals > minorUnits) return { ok: false, error: "At most " + minorUnits + " decimal places" };
  var whole = parts[0];
  var frac = (parts[1] || "").padEnd(minorUnits, "0").slice(0, minorUnits);  // pad
  var digits = (whole === "" ? "0" : whole) + frac;
  // strip leading zeros but keep at least one digit
  digits = digits.replace(/^0+(?=\d)/, "");
  if (digits.length > 15) return { ok: false, error: "Amount too large" };
  return { ok: true, minor: Number(digits) };
}
```
Wait: "15" minor 2 → whole "15", frac "00" → digits "1500" ✓. "15.5" → frac "5"→"50" → "1550" ✓. "15.005" minor 2 → decimals 3 > 2 → reject ✓. minor 0: "15" → frac "" → digits "15" ✓; "15.0" → decimals 1 > 0 reject ✓. ".5" rejected by regex ✓. "15." rejected ✓ (regex needs \d+ after .). "-5" rejected ✓. "1e3" rejected ✓. " 15 " → trim → ok ✓. "15.50" → 1550 ✓. Empty → reject ✓. Leading zeros "015.5" → 1550 ✓ (digits.replace strips to "1550"). Wait "015"+"50" = "01550" → strip leading zero → "1550" ✓. Number("1550") = 1550 ✓.

Precision guard: digits.length > 15 reject → client-side error, no request. Good.

Edge: minorUnits not int (0..3)? Not needed; caller passes server's minor_units.

formatAmount:
```js
function formatAmount(minor, minorUnits, currency) {
  if (typeof minor !== "number" || !isFinite(minor)) minor = 0;
  if (minor < 0) minor = 0;  // R121: balances are never negative; never a minus sign
  var sign = minor < 0 ... (dead)
  var amount = Math.round(minor);  // ints only anyway
  var text;
  if (minorUnits === 0) text = String(amount);
  else {
    var scale = Math.pow(10, minorUnits);
    var whole = Math.floor(amount / scale);
    var frac = String(amount % scale).padStart(minorUnits, "0");
    text = whole + "." + frac;
  }
  return text + " " + currency;
}
```
10000, 2, EUR → "100.00 EUR" ✓. 1200, 0, JPY → "1200 JPY" ✓. 5, 2, EUR → "0.05 EUR" ✓.

createRefreshGuard:
```js
function createRefreshGuard() {
  var issued = 0, applied = 0;
  return {
    issue: function () { issued += 1; return issued; },
    arrive: function (seq) {   // returns true if this response may be rendered
      if (seq <= applied) return false;
      applied = seq;
      return true;
    },
    reset: function () { issued = 0; applied = 0; }
  };
}
```
Test: issue 1, issue 2; arrive(2) → true; arrive(1) → false (dropped, R131). arrive(1) first then arrive(2) → true,true.

