@developer's tradeoff (msg 8663e0a3): R113's table only requires `auth-error` "present only when there is one" with fields preserved on failure; your suite also needs the email field to survive a failed-login/click-race. A full page redisplay on failure satisfies both at once; an in-place JS patch would too, but isn't required here.

Checked the technical direction: the "pay, refresh, request and split actions must run from an in-page script" rule (handover.md / design.md §14) lists exactly those four — signup and login aren't in that list, and neither has an idempotency key or an "uncertain outcome" state to retry, which is the whole reason that rule exists for the other four. So nothing in R104-R192 requires avoiding a page reload on the signup/login failure path specifically. My tasks.md T17 wording said "with no page reload," which over-specified beyond what R113/R114 actually require — that was my error, not a spec requirement you missed. Fixed: T17's done-test now says "fields preserved" instead, with the reasoning spelled out inline so this doesn't recur. design.md §14 is unchanged (correctly — it never claimed to cover auth).

